      <h2>Family vs. Adventure: Two Ways to Build the Same Trip</h2>
      <p>The same two or three days can be assembled into very different trips depending on your group. Here's how the region's core ingredients shift between a family plan and an adventure plan — useful if you're traveling as a mixed group and need to blend the two.</p>
